{"kind":"request","text":"Bound or compact the serialized checkpoint so a checkpoint can still exist at FIRST-PRODUCTION depth.","body":{"conditions":"Measured at main 316d5aeb (docs/reference/performance.md): the checkpoint blob grows about 2,169 B per record on this repository's payload mix (12,552,365 B at 5,786 records) and about 8,526 B per record on the synthetic fixture mix. The 256 MiB ceiling enforced in docs/reference/limits.md is therefore reached near 123,700 records at best and near 31,500 at worst. FIRST-PRODUCTION at 500,000 records needs about 1.06 GiB, 4.2x over the ceiling, so no checkpoint can be written there at all and every restart degrades to the full cold audit (~7.7 h). Suspected bounding component: checkpoint payload is O(depth) with no compaction or truncation. Satisfied when a workroom at 500,000 records can write and load a checkpoint within the 256 MiB ceiling, or the ceiling is deliberately revised with stated reasoning, without weakening what the checkpoint authenticates.","to":"5f12e916d136b0c1ed941aa99f4c47af94021451e31d08159d8df368e9946123"}}